<description>&lt;p&gt;Myanmar’s junta has destroyed bridges in Arakan, moved west of the Sittaung River and is planning a 108‑kilometre fence on the Bangladesh border, while an airstrike hit a displacement camp in Rakhine. In Sagaing, junta forces killed 11 people and Starlink outages isolated communities, and health-care facilities continued to be attacked in October 2026. The International Court of Justice ruled that Myanmar committed genocide against the Rohingya, prompting the junta to reject the verdict as unfair and rights groups to call for sanctions. Rohingya activists say their struggle for justice is still not over after the ruling. There were 2,332 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.euronews.com/2026/11/19/myanmar-guilty-of-genocide-against-rohingya-un-court-rules&quot;&gt;Euronews&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261120-friends-but-who-benefits-notes-from-an-historic-summit-myanmar-s-genocide-ruling-time-to-bre-join-the-eu&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aljazeera.com/video/inside-story/2026/11/20/what-are-the-implications-of-the-icj-rohingya-genocide-ruling?traffic_source=rss&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZkFVX3lxTE5WQ092Rmc5UWx4c3FoUGVaZE1vODQ3V2QwcjF0ZHlkRE00bFlEb0Robmg4aFZ1UWwyVFVOaElXdm9fVi1yR0t1dGRCaE9QZXg1ZUd3Z1Qzc2kwMmJxSlNtaE9hMDQ3Zw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Tamil Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Le Monde.fr&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxOazVmQWNON0pUR1lkMG9ESFlrYjhtOUtQRGNJREZ0cWpPNWIxYTNYaWxjQUN4cUxHU3BVX05BTUc0SlBsblFmQmJ5YjJiOUhHV1RuQTk0OGNLWTFoaWhudm9XS193THFlcU9xbHZqS2w0TGlyOEpRU2Y2dXhDcmFLZXhncDNHa1ctVGFoRFhRcXZROVpYdzZrTWdYbw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Re